WEBVTT

00:08:59.577 --> 00:09:03.289
and children were sent home with no way
of accessing learning resources.

00:09:03.914 --> 00:09:07.376
My team and I took on the challenge
to make learning happen within homes,

00:09:07.418 --> 00:09:09.962
and we produced about 1,000 game packages

00:09:10.004 --> 00:09:12.214
that we gave to teachers
and community leaders.

00:09:12.256 --> 00:09:15.968
And with this, we’re able to help
about 5,000 children

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:19.054
to access home learning
in the most fun and engaging way

00:09:19.096 --> 00:09:20.723
through the use of board games.

00:09:20.723 --> 00:09:24.059
Today, we are working with five schools
in Kyangwali refugee camp

00:09:24.101 --> 00:09:27.187
where we’ve actually been able to work
with school administration

00:09:27.187 --> 00:09:29.815
to make the 5 STA-Z part
of the learning schedules.

00:09:29.857 --> 00:09:31.025
In the morning,